  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "As far as service and number of trips, that is why Issue 7A is so important. Here is an explanation of the different phases of the project. Critically, Phase 1 service is already paid for and underway. However, Phase 2 will be funded by 7A which can expand both the scope of the system and the number of trips provided per day.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "type": "image",
    "version": 1,
    "src": "https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/content/images/2026/10/data-src-image-95f06986-a714-414c-ba13-bcf388423759.png",
    "width": 1903,
    "height": 1057,
    "title": "",
    "alt": "Colorado Connector project phases diagram showing Phase 2 service funded by Issue 7A",
    "caption": "",
    "cardWidth": "regular",
    "href": ""
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "As far as why we need better train infrastructure, here are my main interests:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Continue to provide better, non-highway transportation that connects Colorado’s greatest economic centers.",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "listitem",
        "version": 1,
        "value": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Invest in larger, people-mover type infrastructure. A heavy rail train moving 300-500 people at a time is a solid investment, significantly more than a single bus or light rail train in our urban areas.",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "listitem",
        "version": 1,
        "value": 2
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Enabling and fostering the benefits of denser housing and business development. Expanding on existing hubs like Union Station and Boulder Junction, as well as giving incentives for more transit-oriented development, will be a boon for our cities.",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "listitem",
        "version": 1,
        "value": 3
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Continuing to improve access all-electric transportation options, and reducing our reliance on automobiles for long-distance travel (“",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 8,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "Front Range Passenger Rail could deliver major transportation and environmental benefits",
                "type": "extended-text",
                "version": 1
              }
            ],
            "direction": "ltr",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "type": "link",
            "version": 1,
            "rel": null,
            "target": null,
            "title": null,
            "url": "https://www.swenergy.org/front-range-passenger-rail-could-deliver-major-transportation-and-environmental-benefits/"
          },
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "” — SWEEP)",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "listitem",
        "version": 1,
        "value": 4
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "list",
    "version": 1,
    "listType": "bullet",
    "start": 1,
    "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Boulder has paid significant money for a train. Why should I support 7A?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "As part of Phase 1 for Front Range Passenger Rail, Boulder is getting its train! That’s already paid for in combination with the Regional Transportation District (RTD):",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "The Front Range Passenger Rail District says it already has enough funds to create three round trips a day between Denver and Fort Collins in three years, with the route heading northwest to Boulder and Longmont on the way to Larimer County. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "The $332 million limited phase cost would come from a state transportation innovation fund built up by various fees, and RTD money set aside for FasTracks rail lines north of Denver that were never built. The state and RTD would split the $30 million to $36 million annual operating costs for that phase.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Ballot Issue 7A: Front Range voters will weigh sales tax hike to pay for passenger train service",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://coloradosun.com/2026/09/30/ballot-issue-7a-explained-colorado-train-tax/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " — Colorado Sun",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "However, the biggest risk to Front Range Passenger Rail’s initial implementation is that it will be ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 2,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "underwhelming",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ". Only running three trains per day, with minimal station investment, and not extending the entire length of the proposed system. Voting Yes on 7A will ensure the system is adequately funded over the long term and can bring additional revenue and matching grants to expand the system beyond the initial phase.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "What happens if 7A fails?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "If Issue 7A fails, we’re probably stuck with underwhelming train service, at best. The other issues is that it may jeopardize getting future grants to improve service, such as a ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "$66 million federal grant",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.cpr.org/2024/10/29/colorado-front-range-rail-project-gets-66-million-federal-grant/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " in 2024 used to improve service between Broomfield and Westminster. It’s not clear what the path forward might be if Issue 7A fails.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "How would 7A benefit Boulder and Denver specifically?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Here's a helpful map about where the train would intersect into Boulder. The station will be placed in Boulder Junction, which is a transit-first neighborhood in East Boulder that continues to improve year-over-year. The transit aspect of the neighborhood took a hit since COVID-19 caused the area to lose significant bus service in 2020, which has slowly been improving.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Boulder has pretty excellent transit service along the US 36 / Broadway corridor, but its service to East Boulder is lacking. Providing a long-term boost for residents and businesses in East Boulder could be a solid improvement to make Boulder transit less one-dimensional.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "type": "image",
    "version": 1,
    "src": "https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/content/images/2026/10/data-src-image-54437453-de60-42a2-901c-5804d6fa7626.png",
    "width": 1733,
    "height": 1102,
    "title": "",
    "alt": "Transit map showing how Issue 7A would connect Boulder and Denver with regional rail",
    "caption": "",
    "cardWidth": "regular",
    "href": ""
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Denver is already well-served as the best transit hub in Colorado, but things can still get better. As an anchor to regional train service to Boulder, Fort Collins, Colorado Springs and Pueblo, Denver benefits from a strengthening region, all connected through Denver Union Station.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
